[3841]="70042ED8\n1\tLocate the Haradrim boats\tThe Haradrim boats and supply caches are near the mouth of the River Erui in Lossarnach. First, you should locate the area where the boats and the caches were seen.\n2\tBurn Haradrim boats (total: 7)\030Destroy Haradrim supplies (total: 5)\tThe Haradrim boats and supply caches are near the mouth of the River Erui in Lossarnach. Now that you have discovered the landing area, you should burn their boats and destroy their supply piles.\n3\tTalk to Dagor\tDagor can be found in Arnach, near the keep. You should return to Dagor and tell him how you destroyed the enemy's boats and supplies.\n",
[3842]="70042EDB\n1\tDefeat Haradrim Devoted (total: 12)\tHaradrim invaders can be found east and south of Arnach. You should defeat a number of Haradrim Devoted while they are scattered, so there are fewer to attack in force.\n2\tTalk to Dagor\tDagor can be found in Arnach, near the keep. You should return to Dagor and tell him of the blow you have struck to the foe.\n",
[3843]="7006A1CE\n1\tTalk to Rothog the Storm in the Arena\tRothog awaits you in the Arena.\n2\tTalk to Ezaphir and defeat the first challenge\tEzaphir will issue your first challenge when you are ready to compete.\n3\tTalk to Ezaphir and defeat the second challenge\tEzaphir congratulates you on your success, but he warns you the following challenges may not be so easy.\n4\tTalk to Ezaphir and defeat the third challenge\tEzaphir congratulates you on your victory, but there are more difficult challenges to come.\n5\tTalk to Ezaphir and defeat the fourth challenge\tEzaphir will call forth one of the more stalwart gladiators to test your mettle in glorious combat.\n6\tTalk to Ezaphir and defeat Rothog the Storm\tEzaphir informs you that you are about to face your greatest challenge in the arena: Rothog the Storm himself.\n",
